{
 "summary": "Adds an `interfaces::Block` IPC handle and refactors `BlockTemplate` so `submitSolution()` applies solutions to a copy of the block rather than modifying the template in place. Migrates block retrieval methods (`header()`, `data()`, and `coinbaseMerklePath()`) to the new `Block` interface and changes `submitBlock()` and `submitSolution()` to return a `Block` handle alongside acceptance status. Adds functional tests exercising concurrent template reads and solution submissions.",
 "problem": "Concurrent IPC calls across worker threads can race on `CBlockTemplate` members when `submitSolution()` mutates the template's block in place while another thread reads from it via template getters (issue #36515). Additionally, external IPC callers could not inspect or retain rejected blocks submitted through the interface.",
 "evidence": [
  "Fixes #36515: 'ipc: data race on `m_block_template` members'",
  "Author PR description: 'submitSolution() no longer modifies the template. It applies the solution to a copy of the template block and returns a Block handle for that copy, also when the block is rejected.'"
 ],
