 "scope_notes": "Introduces breaking IPC interface changes in `mining.capnp` (assigning new Cap'n Proto method ordinals and throwing deprecation errors on old ones).",
 "changed_since_previous": "Replaced the previous mutex-locking and `getTotalFees()` approach with an immutable template design using an `interfaces::Block` handle. `submitSolution()` now operates on a copy of the template block rather than mutating the template under a lock.",
 "card": "Adds an interfaces::Block handle and refactors the mining IPC interface so submitSolution operates on a copy instead of modifying the template in place, fixing a concurrent data race between solution submission and template reads (issue #36515). Block retrieval methods are migrated to the Block interface, and submission methods now return a Block handle even when blocks are rejected. This is a breaking change for IPC mining clients (e.g. sv2-tp) using the Cap'n Proto interface.",
